paths: file:BUGS.md file:v1/runtime/backend/rust/src/main/scala/scalascript/codegen/rust/RustCodeWalk.scala file:tests/e2e/rust-match-arm-braces-gate.sh file:tests/e2e/rust-toint-parity-gate.sh file:.github/workflows/ci.yml dir:v1/runtime/backend/rust/src/test
scope: |
  Reduce `rust-multi-statement-match-arm-emitted-without-braces` to a repro, as its own entry
  demands, then take the fix the repro makes falsifiable.

  The reduction lands at 14 lines and refutes the entry's framing: no refusal bypass, no
  `std/json-core.ssc`, no case class. The trigger is a def DECLARED `Any`, whose body-as-match
  renders arms through `renderValueTail` — a statement sequence, spliced straight after `=>`.

  Three defects, each with a control:
    1. the missing braces (`renderMatch` arm assembly) — the reported one;
    2. `subjectIsAny` asked only of a bare `Term.Name`, so a CALL to an `Any`-declared def kept the
       typed path and emitted a struct pattern against a `Value` (E0308). Invisible until 1 was
       fixed, because a parse error stops rustc before type-checking. Filed separately;
    3. a lone match guard wrapped twice — `if ((x > 0i64))` — which had `RustGenControlFlowTest`
       standing red.

  New gate `tests/e2e/rust-match-arm-braces-gate.sh` (4 rows x 3 lanes), wired into ci.yml, with an
  ANTI-ROW that passes with the fix reverted. Two pre-existing reds also cleared, both proved
  pre-existing by control: `backendRust/test` 276/278 -> 278/278, and `rust-toint-parity-gate`'s two
  v2 rows, red on `E0433 num_bigint` — a caller left behind by the cargo migration, third instance.
next: final 17-gate sweep, then commit and push
